iclforge provides CMake targets via find_package(iclforge):

    find_package(iclforge CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE iclforge::ac3)

Every other library is a separate, opt-in feature - none installed by default, since each adds its
own public API, CMake targets and binaries. When present, their own targets are also available:

    matroska  ->  iclforge::containers::matroska                                 (Matroska/.mkv)
    mp4       ->  iclforge::containers::mp4                                      (MP4/ISOBMFF, plus fMP4/CMAF + HLS/DASH)
    mpegts    ->  iclforge::containers::mpegts                                   (MPEG-2 Transport Stream)
    capi      ->  iclforge::c                                        (C11 API over the codecs; AC-4 too with the ac4 feature)
    ac4       ->  iclforge::ac4  (AC-4 decoding, encoding and reading)
    iab       ->  iclforge::iab                                      (SMPTE ST 2098-2 Immersive Audio Bitstream reading)
    iamf      ->  iclforge::containers::iamf                                     (IAMF writing)

    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE iclforge::containers::matroska iclforge::containers::mp4 iclforge::containers::mpegts)

To install the three container writers alongside the codec:

    vcpkg install iclforge[matroska,mp4,mpegts]

Or pick any subset, e.g. AC-4 only:

    vcpkg install iclforge[ac4]
